abstract: >
  RES=RAG is a formal theoretical framework for receptive-generative
  equilibrium in human-machine systems. Version 1.0.0 established the archival
  formal paper and first deterministic CSNP reference profile. Repository
  version 1.1.0 adds a HAL-derived operational extension with signed RES/RAG
  temporal offsets, four-stage semantic-cycle labels, a testable multi-task
  braking intervention, and provenance-labelled research claims while retaining
  local metric-profile calibration and the v1.0.0 scientific boundaries.

